# SaleStudio Event System Audit

## Full Event Map

### 1. `studio:chat`
| | |
|---|---|
| **Dispatched by** | `ActionSyncService` (lines 122, 140) |
| **Received by** | `SaleStudioV2.handleIncomingChat`, `SaleStudio.handleIncomingChat` |
| **Payload** | `{ id, username, content, type, isAI }` |
| **Purpose** | Real-time viewer chat messages. Used to display chat overlay and forward buyer enquiries to Gemini Live. |

---

### 2. `showrunner:directive`
| | |
|---|---|
| **Dispatched by** | [SaleRunner](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/utils/ai/SaleRunner.ts#10-162) (line 131), `NeuralShowrunner` (lines 371, 390, 438, 517, 593, 693, 728, 752) |
| **Received by** | `SyntheticGuestManager.onShowrunnerDirective` (line 182), `SaleStudioV2.handleShowrunnerDirective` (line 732) |
| **Payload** | `{ type, directive, originSpeaker, productContext, gesture?, vibe? }` |
| **Purpose** | Orchestrates what the AI should **say and do next**. The `type` field drives visual clip selection in aidol mode. |

**⚠️ CONFLICT IDENTIFIED:**
`showrunner:directive` is received by **two** listeners simultaneously:
1. `SyntheticGuestManager.onShowrunnerDirective` → calls [notifyWorker('update-3d-expression', { id, gesture: detail.type, productId })](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/utils/ai/SyntheticGuestManager.ts#1356-1359) → dispatches `studio-worker-command`
2. `SaleStudioV2.handleShowrunnerDirective` → handles narrative feed and product highlight

This is **by design** but creates a relay chain: [SaleRunner](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/utils/ai/SaleRunner.ts#10-162) → `showrunner:directive` → [SyntheticGuestManager](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/utils/ai/SyntheticGuestManager.ts#145-1449) → `studio-worker-command` → `SaleStudioV2.handleWorkerCommand` → `renderer.playState()`

---

### 3. `studio-worker-command`
| | |
|---|---|
| **Dispatched by** | `SyntheticGuestManager.notifyWorker()` (line 1357) |
| **Received by** | `VirtualGuest.vue.handleWorkerCommand` (line 343), `SaleStudioV2.handleWorkerCommand` (newly added) |
| **Payload** | `{ type: 'update-3d-expression', payload: { id, gesture, emotion?, productId? } }` or `{ type: 'update-3d-audio', payload: { id, audioLevel } }` or `{ type: 'update-hype-level', payload: { level } }` |
| **Purpose** | Low-level commands to individual renderers. Originally only [VirtualGuest.vue](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/components/studio/virtual/VirtualGuest.vue) listened. In SaleStudioV2 we now also listen to drive the PIXI renderer. |

**Known sub-types:**

| type | Drives |
|------|--------|
| `update-3d-expression` | Sets gesture/emotion/productId on the character |
| `update-3d-audio` | Updates audio level (lip-sync animation) |
| `update-3d-thinking` | Shows thinking indicator |
| `update-hype-level` | Updates hype score for expressions |
| `vision:request_snapshot` | Requests a camera frame for vision AI |

**⚠️ PROBLEM:** In SaleStudioV2, [VirtualGuest.vue](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/components/studio/virtual/VirtualGuest.vue) components are NOT rendered (we use pure PIXI). So the `studio-worker-command` listener on `VirtualGuest` fires with no effect. The new [handleWorkerCommand](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/components/studio/virtual/VirtualGuest.vue#342-365) in SaleStudioV2 is the only path to update the PIXI renderer. This is correct but needs to work properly.

