## Root Cause: Aidol Stuck at Idle

### The Expected Flow (for aidol)
```
SaleRunner.executeCurrentStep()
  └─► window.dispatchEvent('showrunner:directive', { type: step.type, directive, productContext })
        └─► SyntheticGuestManager.onShowrunnerDirective()
              ├─► updates currentDirective, currentVibe
              └─► (aidol only) notifyWorker('update-3d-expression', { id, gesture: detail.type, productId })
                    └─► window.dispatchEvent('studio-worker-command', ...)
                          └─► SaleStudioV2.handleWorkerCommand()
                                └─► renderer.playState(id, gesture, persona, productId)
```

### Problem 1: `step.type` values don't match aidolClips keys

[SaleRunner](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/utils/ai/SaleRunner.ts#10-162) sets `type: step.type || step.gesture || 'product'`

Script steps from SaleWizard use types like `"speaking"`, `"excited"`, `"happy"`, `"victory"` (emotion-based names from the storyboard). But `aidolClips` keys are typically `"idle"`, `"speaking"`, `"product"`, `"checkout"`, etc.

**Fix:** ✅ Already applied — `useSaleRenderer.playState()` now uses a normalization map to resolve aliases.

### Problem 2: Duplicate listener registration causes confusing log spam

From the log, the same tool call appears **4 times** from different HMR versions of [SaleStudioV2.vue](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/views/live/SaleStudioV2.vue):
```
SaleStudioV2.vue?t=1775101775644:467
SaleStudioV2.vue?t=1775112938628:467
SaleStudioV2.vue?t=1775112996475:473
SaleStudioV2.vue:877
```

Each hot-module-reload registers a new `setLiveChatToolCallback` handler without deregistering the old one. **This is an HMR artifact and doesn't occur in production.** However in dev, it causes 4x duplicate tool call processing.

**Fix needed:** Register tool callbacks with a cleanup guard.

### Problem 3: [handleShowrunnerDirective](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/views/live/SaleStudioV2.vue#734-766) in SaleStudioV2 triggers [handleProductHighlight](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/views/live/SaleStudio.vue#561-566) too eagerly

After the user's latest change:
```js
if (detail.productContext) {
    handleProductHighlight(...)
}
```
This fires `studioStore.highlightProduct()` on **every** directive that has a product context, even mid-speech. This may cause the `highlightedProduct` watcher to interrupt the AI by sending a new Gemini prompt ("pitch this product!") when the AI is already pitching.

**Fix needed:** Only call [handleProductHighlight](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/views/live/SaleStudio.vue#561-566) when `detail.type === 'product_showcase'` or it's an explicit user action.

---

## Recommended Cleanup Plan

| Priority | Issue | Fix |
|----------|-------|-----|
| 🔴 High | [handleShowrunnerDirective](file:///d:/Workspace/Gits/CamHub/ams/AntStudio/client/src/views/live/SaleStudioV2.vue#734-766) triggers product pitch on every directive | Re-add `detail.type === 'product_showcase'` guard |
| 🔴 High | HMR duplicate tool call handlers | Add deregistration ID / singleton guard in `AgentEventBus` |
| 🟡 Med | `studio-worker-command` received twice (V2 + no-op VirtualGuest) | No issue in V2 (VirtualGuest not mounted), but wasteful |
| 🟡 Med | SaleRunner dispatches `showrunner:directive` which re-triggers product highlight | NeuralShowrunner does the same; de-duplicate |
| 🟢 Low | `update-3d-audio` not forwarded to PIXI renderer | Add audio-level handler for lip-sync |
